  "body": "## Finding Description and Impact\nThere is a critical inconsistency in the premium exposure calculation formula between token0 and token1 in the `computeNAV()` function in the `PanopticVaultAccountant` contract.\n```solidity\n// Token0 - CORRECT Formula\npoolExposure0 = int256(uint256(shortPremium.rightSlot())) - int256(uint256(longPremium.rightSlot()));\n\n// Token1 - WRONG formula (reverse)\npoolExposure1 = int256(uint256(longPremium.leftSlot())) - int256(uint256(shortPremium.leftSlot()));\n``` \nWhere it should be:\n```solidity\n// Token0\npoolExposure0 = int256(uint256(shortPremium.rightSlot())) - int256(uint256(longPremium.rightSlot()));\n\n// Token1 - FIX\npoolExposure1 = int256(uint256(shortPremium.leftSlot())) - int256(uint256(longPremium.leftSlot()));\n```\nThis will cause vaults with premium positions to experience significant NAV miscalculations. Any vault that has a net positive premium on token1 will lose value in the NAV calculation. Incorrect NAVs can lead to premature or late liquidations.\n\nImpact Scenario\n- Premium Token0: Short 100 ETH, Long 30 ETH → Exposure = +70 ETH ✅\n- Premium Token1: Short 50,000 USDC, Long 20,000 USDC → Exposure = -30,000 USDC ❌ (should be +30,000 USDC)\n- Total Exposure: 70 ETH + (-30,000 USDC) = negative → NAV = 0 (after Math.max)\n- Loss: 30,070 ether in NAV calculation\n\n## Recommended Mitigation Steps\n```diff\n// Calculating pool exposure based on the difference between short and long premiums\n// rightSlot() takes the value of token0, leftSlot() takes the value of token1\npoolExposure0 = int256(uint256(shortPremium.rightSlot())) - int256(uint256(longPremium.rightSlot()));\n- poolExposure1 = int256(uint256(longPremium.leftSlot())) - int256(uint256(shortPremium.leftSlot()));\n+ poolExposure1 = int256(uint256(shortPremium.leftSlot())) - int256(uint256(longPremium.leftSlot()));\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\nMathematical Proof\nScenario Test:\n-\tToken0: Short Premium = 100 ETH, Long Premium = 30 ETH\n-\tToken1: Short Premium = 50,000 USDC, Long Premium = 20,000 USDC\n\nThe calculation should be (Correct):\n-\tToken0 Exposure = 100 - 30 = +70 ETH\n-\tToken1 Exposure = 50,000 - 20,000 = +30,000 USDC\n-\tTotal = +70 ETH + 30,000 USDC = 30,070 (in underlying)\n\nCurrent calculation (Wrong):\n-\tToken0 Exposure = 100 - 30 = +70 ETH ✅\n-\tToken1 Exposure = 20,000 - 50,000 = -30,000 USDC ❌\n-\tTotal = +70 ETH + (-30,000 USDC) = negatif → Math.max(0, negatif) = 0\n\nAdd to `PanopticVaultAccountant.t.sol`.\n```solidity\nfunction testPremiumCalculationLogicError() public {\n    // Setup pools\n    PanopticVaultAccountant.PoolInfo[] memory pools = createDefaultPools();\n    bytes32 poolsHash = keccak256(abi.encode(pools));\n    accountant.updatePoolsHash(vault, poolsHash);\n\n    // Setup scenario with clear premiums to prove the error\n    // Token0 (ETH): Short Premium = 100 ETH, Long Premium = 30 ETH\n    // Token1 (USDC): Short Premium = 50,000 USDC, Long Premium = 20,000 USDC\n    \n    uint256 token0ShortPremium = 100 ether;\n    uint256 token0LongPremium = 30 ether;\n    uint256 token1ShortPremium = 50000 ether;\n    uint256 token1LongPremium = 20000 ether;\n\n    // Setup premium using LeftRightUnsigned\n    // rightSlot = token0, leftSlot = token1\n    LeftRightUnsigned shortPremium = LeftRightUnsigned.wrap(\n        (token1ShortPremium << 128) | token0ShortPremium\n    );\n    LeftRightUnsigned longPremium = LeftRightUnsigned.wrap(\n        (token1LongPremium << 128) | token0LongPremium\n    );\n\n    // Setup mock with predefined premiums\n    mockPool.setMockPremiums(shortPremium, longPremium);\n    mockPool.setNumberOfLegs(vault, 0);\n    mockPool.setMockPositionBalanceArray(new uint256[2][](0));\n\n    // Setup minimal balances to focus on premium calculation\n    token0.setBalance(vault, 0);\n    token1.setBalance(vault, 0);\n    underlyingToken.setBalance(vault, 0);\n    mockPool.collateralToken0().setBalance(vault, 0);\n    mockPool.collateralToken0().setPreviewRedeemReturn(0);\n    mockPool.collateralToken1().setBalance(vault, 0);\n    mockPool.collateralToken1().setPreviewRedeemReturn(0);\n\n    // Create empty tokenIds\n    TokenId[][] memory tokenIds = new TokenId[][](1);\n    tokenIds[0] = new TokenId[](0);\n\n    // Encode manager input\n    bytes memory managerInput = createManagerInput(pools, tokenIds);\n\n    // Calculate NAV with current implementation (which is wrong)\n    uint256 actualNAV = accountant.computeNAV(vault, address(underlyingToken), managerInput);\n\n    // Calculate expected NAV with correct formula\n    // Token0: shortPremium - longPremium = 100 - 30 = 70 ETH\n    int256 expectedToken0Exposure = int256(token0ShortPremium) - int256(token0LongPremium);\n    \n    // Token1: shortPremium - longPremium = 50,000 - 20,000 = 30,000 USDC (CORRECT)\n    int256 expectedToken1Exposure = int256(token1ShortPremium) - int256(token1LongPremium);\n    \n    // Total expected exposure (both positive)\n    int256 expectedTotalExposure = expectedToken0Exposure + expectedToken1Exposure;\n    uint256 expectedNAV = uint256(expectedTotalExposure); // 70 + 30,000 = 30,070\n\n    // Calculate NAV with current implementation (which is wrong)\n    // Token1: longPremium - shortPremium = 20,000 - 50,000 = -30,000 USDC (WRONG!)\n    int256 actualToken1Exposure = int256(token1LongPremium) - int256(token1ShortPremium);\n\n    // Prove that actual result is wrong\n    assertEq(actualNAV, 0, \"NAV should be 0 due to negative exposure from bug\");\n    \n    // Prove that NAV should be 30,070 ether\n    assertTrue(expectedNAV == 30070 ether, \"Expected NAV should be 30,070 ether\");\n    \n    // Prove significant difference due to bug\n    uint256 navDifference = expectedNAV; // because actualNAV = 0\n    assertEq(navDifference, 30070 ether, \"NAV difference due to premium calculation bug\");\n\n    // Prove that token1 exposure is calculated in reverse\n    assertEq(actualToken1Exposure, -30000 ether, \"Token1 exposure incorrectly calculated as negative\");\n    assertEq(expectedToken1Exposure, 30000 ether, \"Token1 exposure should be positive\");\n    \n    // Total difference = 60,000 USDC (30,000 from negative to positive)\n    int256 token1ExposureDifference = expectedToken1Exposure - actualToken1Exposure;\n    assertEq(token1ExposureDifference, 60000 ether, \"Token1 exposure difference is 60,000 due to formula inconsistency\");\n}\n```",
